  "id": "ksads",
  "term": "KSADS",
  "definition": "KSADS is the Kiddie Schedule for Affective Disorders and Schizophrenia, a structured or semi-structured interview used to diagnose psychiatric disorders in children and adolescents, including ADHD. The Present and Lifetime version (KSADS-PL) is described as a gold-standard approach for diagnosis and as a standardized way to identify these conditions.",
